<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid12 .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onDataRange> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/referenceOntologyURI> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Key Performance Indicator (KPI) is a type of semantic description (Genus: owl:Class) that represents a fully specified aggregation computation over instance data of a reference ontology (Differentia specifica).\r\n\r\nGenus: Semantic Description (owl:Class)\r\n\r\nDifferentia specifica:\r\n1. References an external ontology whose instance data serves as the data foundation\r\n2. Specifies a property of the reference ontology over which aggregation is performed\r\n3. Uses exactly one aggregation operator from the controlled vocabulary (e.g., AVG, SUM, COUNT)\r\n4. Can be broken down by 0..n granularity dimensions (GROUP BY)\r\n5. Contains 1..n computed aggregation results, each with their dimension values\r\n\r\nEssential Properties:\r\n- referenceOntologyURI: URI of the reference ontology from which data originates\r\n- aggregationPropertyURI: URI of the property being aggregated\r\n- hasAggregationOperator: The aggregation operator used (exactly one)\r\n- hasGranularityDimension: The dimensions by which results are broken down (0..n)\r\n- hasAggregationResult: The computed result rows (1..n)\r\n- dataSourceURI: Optional URI of the data source (e.g., named graph)\r\n- filterExpression: Optional filter expression to restrict instance data\r\n\r\nRelationships:\r\n- To Aggregation Operator: uses exactly one AggregationOperator\r\n- To Granularity Dimension: has 0..n GranularityDimension instances\r\n- To Aggregation Result: has 1..n AggregationResult instances\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n- KPI \"Average Salary by Gender\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = grossSalary, hasAggregationOperator = Average, hasGranularityDimension = [gender]\r\n- KPI \"Average Salary by Location\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = grossSalary, hasAggregationOperator = Average, hasGranularityDimension = [location]\r\n- KPI \"Employee Count by Location\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = location, hasAggregationOperator = Count, hasGranularityDimension = [location]\r\n\r\nInvariants:\r\n- Must have exactly one referenceOntologyURI\r\n- Must have at least one aggregationPropertyURI\r\n- Must have exactly one hasAggregationOperator\r\n- Must have at least one hasAggregationResult"@en .
<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/> .
<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Key Performance Indicator"@en .
<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Leistungskennzahl"@de .
<https://semantic.adorsys.com/meta/kpi/KeyPerformanceIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eine Leistungskennzahl (KPI) ist eine Art von semantischer Beschreibung (Genus: owl:Class), die eine vollständig spezifizierte Aggregationsberechnung über Instanzdaten einer Referenzontologie repräsentiert (Differentia specifica).\r\n\r\nGenus: Semantische Beschreibung (owl:Class)\r\n\r\nDifferentia specifica:\r\n1. Referenziert eine externe Ontologie, deren Instanzdaten als Datengrundlage dienen\r\n2. Spezifiziert eine Eigenschaft der Referenzontologie, über die aggregiert wird\r\n3. Verwendet genau einen Aggregationsoperator aus dem kontrollierten Vokabular (z.B. AVG, SUM, COUNT)\r\n4. Kann durch 0..n Granularitätsdimensionen aufgeschlüsselt werden (GROUP BY)\r\n5. Enthält 1..n berechnete Aggregationsergebnisse, jeweils mit ihren Dimensionswerten\r\n\r\nWesentliche Eigenschaften:\r\n- referenceOntologyURI: URI der Referenzontologie, aus der die Daten stammen\r\n- aggregationPropertyURI: URI der Eigenschaft, über die aggregiert wird\r\n- hasAggregationOperator: Der verwendete Aggregationsoperator (genau einer)\r\n- hasGranularityDimension: Die Dimensionen, nach denen aufgeschlüsselt wird (0..n)\r\n- hasAggregationResult: Die berechneten Ergebniszeilen (1..n)\r\n- dataSourceURI: Optionale URI der Datenquelle (z.B. Named Graph)\r\n- filterExpression: Optionaler Filterausdruck zur Einschränkung der Instanzdaten\r\n\r\nBeziehungen:\r\n- Zu Aggregationsoperator: verwendet genau einen AggregationOperator\r\n- Zu Granularitätsdimension: hat 0..n GranularityDimension-Instanzen\r\n- Zu Aggregationsergebnis: hat 1..n AggregationResult-Instanzen\r\n\r\nBeispiele:\r\n- KPI \"Durchschnittsgehalt nach Geschlecht\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = grossSalary, hasAggregationOperator = Average, hasGranularityDimension = [gender]\r\n- KPI \"Durchschnittsgehalt nach Standort\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = grossSalary, hasAggregationOperator = Average, hasGranularityDimension = [location]\r\n- KPI \"Anzahl Mitarbeiter nach Standort\": referenceOntologyURI = HROntology, aggregationPropertyURI = location, hasAggregationOperator = Count, hasGranularityDimension = [location]\r\n\r\nInvarianten:\r\n- Muss genau eine referenceOntologyURI haben\r\n- Muss mindestens eine aggregationPropertyURI haben\r\n- Muss genau einen hasAggregationOperator haben\r\n- Muss mindestens ein hasAggregationResult haben"@de .
